00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:09.790
<b>Remind me later</b>

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:09.790
<b>Send a message</b>

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:18.940
Sorry, Fuuka.

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:22.380
<b>You aren't hurt or in trouble 
or anything, are you?</b>

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:31.790
<b>I'm fine</b>

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:31.790
<b>Don't worry. 
It's nothing like that</b>

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:38.150
<b>I was so worried!</b>

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:38.150
<b>I'm glad you responded</b>

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:34.790
<b>I'm fine</b>

00:03:31.790 --> 00:03:34.790
<b>Don't worry. 
It's nothing like that</b>

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:39.530
<b>Sorry</b>

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:36.290
<b>I'm fine</b>

00:03:34.790 --> 00:03:36.290
<b>Don't worry. 
It's nothing like that</b>

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.150
<b>I'm fine</b>

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.150
<b>Don't worry. 
It's nothing like that</b>

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:39.530
<b>What's wrong?</b>

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:52.790
<b>Sorry</b>

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:52.790
<b>What's wrong?</b>

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:52.790
<b>I wanted to see Gama Gama one last time, 
but I couldn't go</b>

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:57.800
<b>I want some time off</b>

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.300
Did she respond?

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:03.320
Yes.

00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.800
She seems to be safe.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.220
Okay.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:08.840
Her presentation didn't go well.

00:04:08.840 --> 00:04:10.490
I wonder if she's depressed.

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:12.030
I might have pressured her too much

00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:14.500
when I lectured her about the joys 
of work and stuff.

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.150
She'll be all right.

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:17.420
I think.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.800
She's just a bit tired.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.380
She's fine.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:30.180
<b>I wanted to see Gama Gama 
one last time, but I couldn't go</b>

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:30.180
<b>I want some time off</b>

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:30.180
<b>I'll talk to the assistant director</b>

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:30.180
<b>Go ahead and take a break</b>

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.910
<b>I'm glad you're safe</b>

00:04:33.140 --> 00:04:35.990
Seriously, what am I doing?

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.180
Kukuru-chan?

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.800
I thought so!

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.640
It's been a while, huh?

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:51.820
Misaki-san?

00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:55.910
Whoops.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:58.810
Thanks.

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:02.810
That's your wife, right?

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:03.760
Yup.

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:05.550
You said she's on the smaller islands.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:07.240
What does she do?

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.120
She's an associate professor.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.950
She studies sea turtles.

00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:13.450
Brilliant.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:18.790
We're both so obsessed with work 
that we rarely see each other.

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:25.090
It's been such a long time.

00:05:25.360 --> 00:05:29.800
You've been working with Gou-chan 
since Gama Gama closed, right?

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:31.220
Gou-chan?

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:34.020
Oh.

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:41.430
Are you over here for work?

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:46.910
There's a tiny little aquarium here, too, 
called Kamehausu.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:48.440
Oh, yeah.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:51.440
I thought that's why you were here.

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:52.990
Not necessarily.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.620
Is something wrong?

00:06:00.120 --> 00:06:02.630
Work isn't going too well.

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.230
I see.

00:06:04.840 --> 00:06:07.850
I came to run away.

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:09.510
Yeah?

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:13.370
Well, now that you've run away, 
you might as well enjoy it more.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:16.700
You're going to get yelled at later, anyway.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:19.320
There's no sense being sad about it yet.

00:06:19.320 --> 00:06:20.650
It's a huge waste.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:22.700
You tried hard, and it didn't work out, 
so take a break.

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.590
Reflect after you've taken a break.

00:06:24.590 --> 00:06:26.760
And get back to work 
after you've reflected some.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:29.530
You can't do all that 
at the same time. Right?

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:35.870
Where are you staying, Kukuru-chan?

00:06:35.870 --> 00:06:37.790
I haven't decided yet.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:40.370
You should come where I'm staying, then.

00:06:40.620 --> 00:06:42.520
They said there's a room open.

00:06:43.010 --> 00:06:47.270
Well, now that that's settled, 
let's tend to some business.

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.390
<b>Please don't go past the fence</b>

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:55.390
<b>We are protecting sea turtle eggs.
Please do not play in or leave things in this area.
Vehicle tires can hurt sea turtle eggs and young.
We ask for your cooperation to ensure 
the sea turtles can return safely to the water.

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:02.900
By "business," you meant picking up litter?

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:08.570
This kind of driftage can get in the way 
when hatchlings try to return to sea.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.280
They're born here?

00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:11.520
Yeah.

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:15.200
They came to shore 50 days ago 
and laid their eggs.

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:19.020
Ideal solar conditions, 
perfect accumulated temperature.

00:07:19.020 --> 00:07:22.920
Once you start seeing dents in the sand, 
they start hatching.

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:26.170
I've never seen sea turtles hatch.

00:07:26.700 --> 00:07:30.410
We never did artificial incubation 
at either Gama Gama or Tingarla.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:32.380
You'll be blown away, then!

00:07:32.380 --> 00:07:35.840
The ground wells up as if it's erupting.

00:07:35.840 --> 00:07:37.430
And the baby turtles come springing out!

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:42.960
They march forward, 
toward the light of the sea.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:48.970
When you see it, it makes you realize that 
that's the moment you've been working for.

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:54.200
I can put up with anything, 
if it's for the animals.

00:07:55.890 --> 00:07:59.750
Come on! At least pick up some garbage 
if you're going to be staring at your feet.

00:07:59.750 --> 00:08:02.710
Dinner will taste better 
if you get plenty of exercise.

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:05.210
She's sick?

00:08:05.690 --> 00:08:06.700
Yes.

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:10.960
She has a fever and says
 she has a stomachache.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.860
So, um...

00:08:12.860 --> 00:08:15.470
Basically, she's fake sick.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:16.970
She's not!

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:19.100
It's true that she's not feeling well.

00:08:19.390 --> 00:08:20.890
Absent without notice.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:24.750
She's working on a project right now, 
and the new area is opening soon.

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:27.310
I'll make up for Kukuru!

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:30.620
Your job isn't to take care of Misakino.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:33.200
We'll deal with this ourselves.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.780
Go back to your own work.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:42.410
He didn't have to say it like that!

00:08:42.410 --> 00:08:43.080
Jeez!

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:50.340
I'm sorry!

00:08:50.840 --> 00:08:53.340
No, was that a Kukuru impression?

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:54.730
Kukuru?

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:57.790
Oh, uh, nothing.

00:08:57.790 --> 00:09:00.710
Speaking of which, 
is Misakino-san off work today?

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.350
Someone from the equipment team told me.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:05.870
People love talking about her.

00:09:05.870 --> 00:09:09.740
She pops up everywhere. 
The Cryptid Behind the Scenes.

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:11.190
"Cryptid"?

00:09:11.500 --> 00:09:13.910
There's a lot of cryptid fans 
out there, you know.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:18.200
<b>Hotel Bougainvillea</b>

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.200
Your room's upstairs.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.960
And here are your sheets.

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:21.200
I'll be in your care.

00:09:21.720 --> 00:09:23.640
They won't hatch overnight.

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:25.440
Get plenty of rest.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:26.710
Thanks.

00:09:52.870 --> 00:09:54.260
So pretty.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:02.360
Gama Gama...

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:04.570
I want to go back.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:09.000
<b>Dreams of Blue Turtles</b>

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:27.680
Good morning.

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:29.260
Morning.

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:30.900
Did you sleep well?

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:33.270
I overslept.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:36.430
Nothing wrong with getting plenty of sleep.

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:38.030
Hey, have you seen Misaki-san?

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:41.210
Oh, what was it that she said...

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:44.680
Oh, right. "Fieldwork."

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:48.460
You must be hungry.

00:10:48.460 --> 00:10:49.120
Here.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:52.420
Thank... you.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.970
I made lots.

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:57.140
Eat well.

00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:05.680
Is Kamehausu close by?

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:09.690
It's still here!

00:11:09.690 --> 00:11:12.310
You should keep it at the aquarium.

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:17.690
It's got family in the ocean.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:21.820
You wouldn't want to be separated 
from your family, would you?

00:11:22.200 --> 00:11:24.400
Gramps. Why are you here?

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:26.240
I have time to spare.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:28.290
So I come check on it sometimes.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.160
It doesn't seem to be weakening.

00:11:31.160 --> 00:11:35.280
Yes, but it's just been going back 
and forth around there.

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:38.550
Maybe it had a terrifying experience.

00:11:40.790 --> 00:11:46.380
Oh, the Gama Gama kids are moving 
to Tingarla soon.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:11:48.310
Choko and the gang.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:51.230
Tell Kukuru for me.

00:11:51.230 --> 00:11:53.370
I'm sure she'll be happy.

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:54.760
Okay.

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>Big news!</b>

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:04.070
<b>Gramps just told me that Choko 
and the others are coming to Tingarla.</b>

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:07.950
Fuuka!

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:10.490
Let's do Shiratama's checkup.

00:12:10.490 --> 00:12:11.790
Okay.

00:12:13.820 --> 00:12:15.880
3,220 grams.

00:12:16.270 --> 00:12:17.680
No problem there.

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:19.760
Sorry, you're almost done.

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.060
I want to give her some space.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:35.110
I should wait until she's back 
to tell her about Choko, right?

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:45.450
Popo!

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:50.660
From the base of the beak and the back.

00:12:51.180 --> 00:12:53.410
It looks like the back's
been pecked pretty bad.

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:56.620
Okay.

00:12:58.280 --> 00:12:59.140
Okay.

00:13:00.420 --> 00:13:01.310
Okay!

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:02.810
Please and thank you!

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:04.300
I got some bandages.

00:13:04.590 --> 00:13:06.970
Thank you, Gyarandou-san!

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:08.300
It's "Garandou."

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:11.120
Popo's so curious.

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:13.470
They must have wandered 
into someone else's territory.

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:15.350
I should have been paying attention.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:16.880
It's all right.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.520
Penguins get into fights all the time.

00:13:19.520 --> 00:13:21.400
You don't have to worry about it.

00:13:23.480 --> 00:13:24.650
Okay.

00:14:22.340 --> 00:14:25.440
Green caviar Gorigori-kun 
is the best Gorigori-kun!

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:27.050
Nah man, bitter gourd pudding!

00:14:27.050 --> 00:14:28.780
No! Soda!

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:30.050
No way!

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:32.050
<b>Kamehausu</b>

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.560
It's even smaller than Gama Gama.

