It's pretty big inside.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:12.590
<b>Do porcupine fish actually have 1000 needles?</b>

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:12.590
<b>Ojisan 
(that's its actual name)</b>

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.600
<b>Creatures of the Reef</b>

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.600
<b>Blue-green puller</b>

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.600
<b>Threadfin butterflyfish</b>

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.600
<b>Blue damselfish</b>

00:15:12.590 --> 00:15:14.600
<b>Bird wrasse</b>

00:15:12.940 --> 00:15:14.600
It's kind of similar.

00:15:14.600 --> 00:15:16.350
To Gama Gama.

00:15:16.350 --> 00:15:17.770
Hello there.

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:19.270
Welcome.

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:20.860
Thanks for having me.

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:23.590
You're a guest. You can relax.

00:15:23.590 --> 00:15:26.630
Oh, hey, you found that, huh?

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.030
<b>Today's Mission</b>

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:27.030
<b>Find the Reef Stonefish!</b>

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:29.840
It's camouflaged with the rocks.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:32.900
You get a coral decoration 
if you can find it.

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:34.670
Hey, Yama!

00:15:34.670 --> 00:15:35.130
Hey.

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:37.040
It's the reef stonefish today?

00:15:37.040 --> 00:15:39.040
Find it! Find it!

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:45.870
I found the reef stonefish!

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:46.990
Over here, too!

00:15:46.990 --> 00:15:48.420
That was fast.

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:50.670
Let's see...

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:53.000
Yep, correct.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:54.800
Help yourselves to a ice cream.

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:57.500
Yay! That was so easy!

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:58.430
Ice cream?

00:15:58.430 --> 00:16:01.150
The kids don't want the coral.

00:16:01.150 --> 00:16:03.180
So we draw them 
with ice cream instead.

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:06.890
But they get faster and faster 
at finding them.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:08.650
They're here for the ice cream, huh?

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:09.930
It's fine.

00:16:09.930 --> 00:16:11.400
Anything that gets them to come in.

00:16:11.980 --> 00:16:15.620
As long as it gets them to love fish.

00:16:16.670 --> 00:16:21.320
Actually, I just stole that line 
from a great mentor of mine.

00:16:22.490 --> 00:16:23.990
Enjoy your stay.

00:16:25.890 --> 00:16:28.550
Of course, the legendary aquarium keeper.

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:36.140
<b>Japanese eel catfish</b>

00:16:34.050 --> 00:16:37.050
<b>Lionfish</b>

00:16:42.530 --> 00:16:43.820
Found it.

00:16:49.320 --> 00:16:50.910
Hang in there!

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:51.820
There.

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:54.380
Now let's keep an eye on them for a while.

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:58.590
We might not want to let
them out for a few days.

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:03.550
If they're having a hard time eating, 
chop up or mince the feed.

00:17:03.550 --> 00:17:05.290
Make sure they don't lose weight.

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:06.170
Okay.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.830
Thank you.

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:11.960
Were you that worried?

00:17:11.960 --> 00:17:17.480
It hurts my heart to see animals suffer.

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:20.720
I can't stand not being able 
to do anything for them.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:24.480
That goes for vets and attendants alike.

00:17:24.480 --> 00:17:26.940
We can't communicate with them in words,

00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:30.300
so it's hard to know what to do for them.

00:17:31.040 --> 00:17:33.740
Especially when one passes 
after I've been taking care of them.

00:17:36.290 --> 00:17:39.240
You don't have to worry so much.

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.930
They'll recover just fine with some care.

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:44.100
You don't need to be watching them all day.

00:17:44.100 --> 00:17:45.060
Okay.

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:49.400
There's no time to be regretting things 
when you're dealing with animals.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.500
Don't wallow. Struggle!

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:54.280
Don't wallow?

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.890
<b>AM: Came up to ask for food. Gave them 5 fish. 
Asked for more, so gave them 2 more.</b>

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.890
<b>12:00 approx: Peeped into a nest near the staff area entrance, 
got pecked on by several excited penguins around the right eye and back, 
leading to bleeding. We cleaned the areas and stopped the bleeding, and called 
Dr. Takeshita just in case. We've covered the cartilage for safety, and will be keeping 
an eye on them for several days. No appetite issues so far. 
Will force feed if they don't eat. If they still don't eat, 
we'll mince food and feed directly using a catheter.</b>

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.890
<b>Notes</b>

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.890
<b>Popo was injured even though I was nearby. I was too busy taking care 
of Shiratama to notice there was a problem.</b>

00:18:04.890 --> 00:18:07.640
<b>To prevent this from happening again...</b>

00:18:08.530 --> 00:18:10.840
What could I do?

00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:12.150
There you are.

00:18:12.750 --> 00:18:14.150
Umi-yan-san.

00:18:14.150 --> 00:18:16.190
I found out where Kukuru-chan is.

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:18.680
She's with my wife.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:21.390
She seems to be doing well.

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:22.650
You can relax.

00:18:22.650 --> 00:18:24.330
Where is she?

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:25.680
It's fine.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:28.030
I've been giving you plenty 
of trouble anyway.

00:18:28.030 --> 00:18:30.080
We'll take care of Popo!

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:32.290
Thank you!

00:18:40.630 --> 00:18:41.910
Come in.

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:45.280
I heard you checked out the aquarium.

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:46.680
Yama-chan told me.

00:18:47.150 --> 00:18:47.900
Yeah.

00:18:47.900 --> 00:18:49.790
I even got a gift.

00:18:49.790 --> 00:18:51.060
They're hatching.

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:53.230
Tonight.

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:56.840
My students saw the indicators.

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:11.930
It's a perfect night for hatching.

00:19:11.930 --> 00:19:14.170
The waves are nice and calm, too.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:15.950
This is Yamahara-san.

00:19:15.950 --> 00:19:19.260
He helps out with research 
at my university every year.

00:19:19.260 --> 00:19:21.150
We met during the day, didn't we?

00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:23.760
Thank you for the coral decoration.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:28.520
Yama-chan works as a tour guide around this time 
of the year, when the turtles hatch.

00:19:28.800 --> 00:19:30.890
Sensei, it's starting.

00:19:31.410 --> 00:19:34.910
Please don't shine light on them 
with your phones or flashlights!

00:19:34.910 --> 00:19:38.900
The hatchlings will be
drawn to them and get lost.

00:19:39.280 --> 00:19:43.410
And please be careful 
not to stand in their way!

00:20:09.260 --> 00:20:11.350
Huh? They aren't moving.

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:15.840
Don't worry.

00:20:15.840 --> 00:20:21.850
These kids know what they need to do, 
and where they need to go.

00:20:22.310 --> 00:20:25.200
They're just saving up their
strength in the sand.

00:20:25.770 --> 00:20:27.560
For when they start running.

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:32.660
You can do it.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.410
It's amazing.
